  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only with scvi_n200, multiprofile, and avgpool is the best configuration so far (0.650 accuracy), and the only multimodal test with the same RNA settings plus resnet50 and concat fusion is slightly lower (0.632 accuracy). This leaves uncertainty about whether the small multimodal drop is due to concat fusion or the image encoder itself. config_031 changes only fusion from concat to weighted while keeping scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, and resnet50 fixed, so it isolates the fusion effect. It is the best next experiment because it directly tests whether the promising scvi/multiprofile/avgpool direction can be made multimodal with a better fusion rule before spending limited budget on less-supported image encoders or aggregation changes."
}

